# @aegis/identity
# Copy to `.env.local`. Never commit a filled-in copy.

# ── Public — inlined into the browser bundle. Nothing secret may live here.

# The identity API. This MUST be the same origin the portals send their session
# cookie to — an identity app pointed at a different API would mint sessions
# nothing else recognises.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:5000/api/v1"

# Where "back to the website" goes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBSITE_URL="http://localhost:3100"

NEXT_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT="development"

# ── The API's own settings (set these on the backend, not here) ──────────────
#
# Listed for reference because they decide what this app can do:
#
#   IDENTITY_APP_URL          where emailed links point — must be THIS app
#   CUSTOMER_PORTAL_URL       where a CUSTOMER realm sign-in lands
#   EMPLOYEE_PORTAL_URL       where an EMPLOYEE realm sign-in lands
#   ENTERPRISE_PORTAL_URL     where an ENTERPRISE realm sign-in lands
#   PLATFORM_ADMIN_URL        where a PLATFORM realm sign-in lands
#   WORKSPACE_EMAIL_DOMAINS   comma-separated domains a staff realm accepts a
#                             provider sign-in from. This is the whole of what
#                             separates "Google" from "Google Workspace".
#                             Empty means NO domain qualifies, so a staff realm
#                             refuses everybody until it is set — a visible
#                             misconfiguration rather than an open door.
#   AUTH_MAIL_WEBHOOK_URL     where verification and reset mail is delivered.
#                             Unset, the message is written to the server log
#                             with a warning; in production the link itself is
#                             withheld from that log.
